    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION If you invest in our Securities, assuming\nno value is attributed to the related Warrants, your interest will be diluted to the extent of the difference between the initial public\noffering price per Common Share included in the Unit and our net tangible book value per Common Share immediately after this offering.\nDilution results from the fact that the assumed initial public offering price per Common Share included in the Unit is substantially\nin excess of the net tangible book value per Common Share attributable to the existing shareholders for our presently outstanding Common\nShares. Our net tangible book value was approximately\nC$0.31, or approximately US$0.22 per Common Share, as of June 30, 2026. Our net tangible book value represents the amount of our total\nconsolidated tangible assets, less the amount of our total consolidated liabilities. Dilution is determined by subtrac",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
